# Directories Bazel must not descend into when resolving a target pattern
# like //... .
#
# These are the bazel-* convenience symlinks that get created in a directory
# that is (or once was) a workspace root of its own. c_little_book/ used to be
# a separate workspace; the marker is gone but its symlinks pointed at a stale
# output base, and //... would recurse into it and fail during package loading
# with an unresolvable @apple_support / local_config_cc error. Bazel skips
# those symlinks automatically at the repo root, but not in a subdirectory.
#
# Entries must be exact paths relative to the workspace root -- .bazelignore
# does not support wildcards (verified against Bazel 9.2.0: both */bazel-* and
# **/bazel-* are silently ignored). So if another area ever sprouts its own
# bazel-* symlinks, add its four paths here explicitly.
c_little_book/bazel-bin
c_little_book/bazel-c_little_book
c_little_book/bazel-out
c_little_book/bazel-testlogs
